  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_honor_killing_claim",
  "label": "The speaker's claim about honor killings is mapped onto the visual of the man shouting in protest.",
  "description": "The text 'honor killings are part of our culture' is directly overlaid on the image of the man shouting in protest. This creates an analogical mapping where the man's visual representation (his angry expression, raised fists, and protest setting) is being used to embody or represent the speaker of the claim. The visual material (man_shouting) is mapped onto the textual material (text_chunk_1) to convey that the man is the one making the claim about honor killings being part of culture.",
